---
import Plate from '../../plate/Plate.astro';
import { renderFormula } from '../../../lib/formulas/render';
import { HALF_GAPS, ONE_GAPS, NUMERICAL_GAP, CLAIMED_BOUNDS } from './math';
import { CUES, FILM_DURATION, formatTime } from './story';
import './gap-ladder.css';

const formula = (tex: string) => renderFormula(tex, false);

const escape = (text: string) => text.replaceAll('&', '&amp;').replaceAll('<', '&lt;').replaceAll('>', '&gt;');

function subtitle(text: string): string {
  const pieces = text.split('$');

  return pieces.map((piece, index) => {
    if (index % 2 === 0) return escape(index > 0 ? piece.replace(/^\S+/, '') : piece);

    const attached = /^\S+/.exec(pieces[index + 1] ?? '')?.[0] ?? '';

    return `<span class="glfilm-phrase">${formula(piece)}${escape(attached)}</span>`;
  }).join('');
}

const labels = [
  { id: 'bond-pure', tex: String.raw`h=\mathbf S_j\cdot\mathbf S_{j+1}`, blue: false },
  { id: 'bond-aklt', tex: String.raw`h+\tfrac13h^2`, blue: false },
  { id: 'floor60', tex: String.raw`\tfrac4{105}\log\tfrac{80}{79}`, blue: true },
  { id: 'floor2304', tex: String.raw`\tfrac{\log20}{784}`, blue: true },
  { id: 'floor-open', tex: String.raw`\tfrac{\log10}{392}`, blue: true },
  { id: 'purity-lemma', tex: String.raw`1-P'\le\frac{u^2}{2(1-u)^2}`, blue: false },
  { id: 'purity-gap', tex: String.raw`\frac1b\log\frac{T}{1-T}`, blue: true },
  { id: 'partition', tex: 'Z_n(b)', blue: false },
  { id: 'transfer', tex: 'X_b', blue: false },
  { id: 'physical-purity', tex: String.raw`T=\frac{Z_n(2b)}{Z_n(b)^2}`, blue: false },
  { id: 'spatial-purity', tex: String.raw`S=\frac{Z_{2n}(b)}{Z_n(b)^2}`, blue: false },
  { id: 'defect', tex: String.raw`C^{-1}r^{2^j}`, blue: true },
  { id: 'b', tex: 'b', blue: false },
  { id: 'step-weights', tex: String.raw`\lvert\lambda_i\rvert^n`, blue: false },
];

const ring = Array.from({ length: 8 }, (_, index) => {
  const angle = -Math.PI / 2 + index * Math.PI / 4;

  return { x: 150 + 96 * Math.cos(angle), y: 145 + 96 * Math.sin(angle), up: index % 2 === 0 };
});

const chartX = (length: number) => length <= 24 ? 34 + (length - 4) / 20 * 168 : 202 + Math.log(length / 24) / Math.log(2304 / 24) * 74;

const chartY = (gap: number) => 215 - gap / 1.1 * 165;
---

<Plate
  caption="A ring of quantum magnets and its ladder of energies; the gap, computed for small rings, closing for spin one half and levelling off for spin one; and the claimed proof that it never closes for spin one, which squares two distributions hidden in one number."
  leftOut="the earlier extensions and perturbation results; how White and Huse computed; the ordered bond expansion, symmetry sectors and energy shift; the coupled update's constants and interpolation exponent; the conditioned Poisson polynomial and interval enclosures; matrix-product energies and thermodynamic limits; the open-chain boundary update and topological index; odd rings, free ends, other fields and higher spins. The proof drawings are schematic."
>
  <uruk-gap-ladder>
    <div class="glfilm">
      <div class="glfilm-stage" data-film-viewport>
        <canvas class="glfilm-canvas" data-film-canvas role="img" aria-label="A film of a ring of quantum magnets and its energy ladder. Computed gaps for small rings are compared with three claimed lower bounds. The proof is illustrated through two probability distributions and repeated doubling. A complete text transcript follows."></canvas>
        <div class="glfilm-still" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="glfilm-still-ring">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 300 300" role="presentation">
              <text x="150" y="17" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="12">A RING OF 8 · SPIN ONE</text>
              <circle cx="150" cy="145" r="96" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1" />
              {ring.map((site) => (
                <>
                  <circle cx={site.x} cy={site.y} r="12" fill="var(--paper)" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.1" />
                  {[0, 1, 2].map((notch) => <line x1={site.x + 8 * Math.cos(Math.PI * notch / 2)} y1={site.y - 8 * Math.sin(Math.PI * notch / 2)} x2={site.x + 11 * Math.cos(Math.PI * notch / 2)} y2={site.y - 11 * Math.sin(Math.PI * notch / 2)} stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1" />)}
                  <line x1={site.x} y1={site.y} x2={site.x} y2={site.y + (site.up ? -8 : 8)} stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.5" />
                  <circle cx={site.x} cy={site.y} r="1.5" fill="var(--ink)" />
                </>
              ))}
              <text x="150" y="269" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="15">Computed gap: {ONE_GAPS[2].toFixed(6)}</text>
              <text x="150" y="291" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="10">NEEDLES ARE A PICTURE OF QUANTUM SPINS</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="glfilm-still-chart">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 330 300" role="presentation">
              <text x="165" y="15" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="11">GAP ABOVE THE LOWEST ENERGY</text>
              <text x="165" y="34" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="12">Hollow: spin ½ · Filled: spin 1</text>
              <line x1="34" y1="50" x2="34" y2="215" stroke="var(--muted)" />
              <line x1="34" y1="215" x2="310" y2="215" stroke="var(--muted)" />
              {[0, .5, 1].map((gap) => <text x="25" y={chartY(gap) + 4} text-anchor="end" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="11">{gap}</text>)}
              {HALF_GAPS.map((gap, index) => <circle cx={chartX(4 + 2 * index)} cy={chartY(gap)} r="3.5" fill="var(--paper)" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1" />)}
              {ONE_GAPS.map((gap, index) => <circle cx={chartX(4 + 2 * index)} cy={chartY(gap)} r="2.3" fill="var(--ink)" />)}
              <line x1={chartX(14)} y1={chartY(ONE_GAPS[5])} x2="304" y2={chartY(NUMERICAL_GAP)} stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-dasharray="3 3" />
              <text x="218" y={chartY(NUMERICAL_GAP) - 13} text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="12">0.41050 · numerical</text>
              <path d={`M${chartX(60)} ${chartY(CLAIMED_BOUNDS.periodic60)}H304M${chartX(2304)} ${chartY(CLAIMED_BOUNDS.periodic2304)}H304`} fill="none" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1.2" />
              <path d={`M${chartX(1921)} ${chartY(CLAIMED_BOUNDS.open1921)}H304`} fill="none" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width="1.1" stroke-dasharray="3 2" />
              <path d="M204 211L209 219M209 211L214 219" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width=".8" />
              {[4, 14, 24, 60, 2304].map((length) => <text x={chartX(length)} y="231" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="10">{length}</text>)}
              <text x="307" y="231" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="13">∞</text>
              <text x="165" y="249" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--muted)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="10">RING LENGTH · LOG SCALE AFTER THE BREAK</text>
              <text x="165" y="269" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--blue)" font-family="var(--font-alegreya)" font-size="12">Claimed positive floors, far below 0.41</text>
              <rect x="65" y="281" width="200" height="17" fill="var(--paper)" stroke="var(--blue)" stroke-width=".8" stroke-dasharray="3 2" />
              <text x="165" y="293" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--blue)" font-family="var(--font-special-elite)" font-size="11">CLAIMED · UNDER REVIEW</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="glfilm-formulas" aria-hidden="true" data-bleed>
          {labels.map((label) => <span class:list={['glfilm-label', 'glfilm-label--small', { 'glfilm-label--blue': label.blue }]} data-label={label.id}><span set:html={formula(label.tex)} /></span>)}
          <span class="glfilm-label glfilm-status" data-label="status"><span>CLAIMED · UNDER REVIEW</span></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="glfilm-subtitles" aria-hidden="true">
        {CUES.map((cue, index) => <p class:list={['glfilm-cue', { 'is-active': index === 0 }]} data-cue={index}><span set:html={subtitle(cue.text)} /><span class="glfilm-citations"> {cue.sources.map((source) => `[${source}]`).join('')}</span></p>)}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="glfilm-controls" data-script-only>
      <div class="glfilm-buttons">
        <button class="plate-button case-link case-link--tight" type="button" data-play><span data-play-label>Pause</span></button>
        <p class="glfilm-clock"><span data-film-clock>0:00 / {formatTime(FILM_DURATION)}</span></p>
        <button class="plate-button case-link case-link--tight" type="button" data-film-restart>Restart</button>
      </div>
      <label class="visually-hidden" for="glfilm-timeline">Film timeline. Arrow keys move one subtitle at a time.</label>
      <input id="glfilm-timeline" class="glfilm-timeline" data-film-range type="range" min="0" max={FILM_DURATION} step="100" value="0" />
      <div class="glfilm-steps">
        <button class="plate-button case-link case-link--tight" type="button" data-film-previous>Previous</button>
        <p>Step through without motion</p>
        <button class="plate-button case-link case-link--tight" type="button" data-film-next>Next</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="visually-hidden" data-film-status aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
    <details class="glfilm-transcript">
      <summary class="text-link">Read the film as text</summary>
      <ol>{CUES.map((cue) => <li><h3>{cue.title}</h3><p><span set:html={subtitle(cue.text)} /> {cue.sources.map((source) => <> <a class="citation text-link" href={`#source-${source}`}>[{source}]</a></>)}</p></li>)}</ol>
      <p class="glfilm-method">How the film is made. The plotted small-ring gaps were computed by Lanczos iteration for spin one half at lengths 4 through 20 and spin one at lengths 4 through 14. The spin-one ring of eight has 6,561 states. Its complete diagonalization, grouped into 683 distinct levels, supplies the energy ladder, degeneracies, energy weights and purities. Intermediate ladder positions carry the object between computed rings; they are not additional spectral calculations. The dashed 0.41050 line is White and Huse's 1993 numerical estimate, cited by the article.</p>
      <p class="glfilm-method">The needles illustrate quantum spins; they are not classical directions or a computed quantum state. The AKLT halves and pairs picture its valence-bond construction. The sheet, bond-history marks, transfer cursor and step weights are schematic. The film does not compute the eigenvalues of the spatial transfer operator. Its energy weights are computed from all 6,561 states and normalized at each inverse temperature b. Raising b cools the system. The bar for all other states groups their weight for display; the purity still uses the separate states.</p>
      <p class="glfilm-method">Squaring and renormalizing physical energy weights doubles b exactly. The physical and spatial purities share the same partition functions, which is why the proof can couple doubling in both directions. The film uses the paper's exact starting sequence, while leaving the uncomputed constants C and r as letters.</p>
      <p class="glfilm-method">The gap-from-purity illustration is an elementary consequence of the weights. The largest weight is at least the purity T, and every other weight is at most 1 − T. Thus T &gt; 1/2 forces a unique lowest state and gives <span set:html={formula(String.raw`\gamma\ge\frac1b\log\frac{T}{1-T}`)} />. On the ring of eight at b = 16 the bound is about 0.482, below its computed gap of about 0.594. This illustrates the argument; it is not the paper's uniform lower bound. The blue steps are the papers' claimed bounds for their specified even rings and odd open chains with endpoint field 3/5. They do not claim the numerical value 0.41050.</p>
      <p class="glfilm-method">Tasaki's review covers the analytic argument. The article records that he has not independently checked the computer-assisted estimates. The finite calculations used for the film do not validate those certificates or the proof for arbitrarily long rings.</p>
    </details>
  </uruk-gap-ladder>
</Plate>

<script>
  import './element';
</script>
